  "body": "Fork synced at v0.17.0.\n\n## What changed\nWhen `ruststep` rejects a STEP file it fails the whole DATA section and its position is not the bad entity (#887). `step_diag::locate` (new, `crates/app/src/geometry/import/step_diag.rs`) now re-scans the text once after a parse failure: records split on `;` outside `'..'` strings and `/* */` comments, line numbers tracked, DATA..ENDSEC followed, each record parsed alone with ruststep's `entity_instance`. The first failing record is named. Unterminated strings/comments name the line they opened on; a file with no DATA section says so. If every record parses alone, ruststep's own message is kept. Linear in file size (each byte visited once, each record parsed once); no unwrap/expect/panic. ruststep is not patched.\n\n## Error text\n- Old: `syntax error: <ruststep position, at the DATA section>`\n- New: `syntax error in DATA section: entity #9 at line 16 cannot be parsed: #9 = PRODUCT_DEFINITION_CONTEXT('part definition' #2, 'design')`\n- Also: `syntax error: comment starting at line 6 is never closed`, `syntax error: no DATA section found`.\n\n## Tests (crates/app/tests/import.rs)\n`step_parse_error_names_the_bad_entity_and_line` (hand-made fixture `testdata/models/bad_entity_mid_data.step`, empty_list.step with one comma removed), `step_parse_error_line_survives_strings_and_comments`, `step_parse_error_unterminated_and_no_data`. Gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green on the final head; clippy `-D warnings` on camcraft-app clean.\n\n## Not exercised\nReal HOOPS Exchange file from #887 (vendor files are not committed); multi-GB files; complex-entity (`#n = ( A() B() );`) failures beyond the shared per-record parser.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/912-step-error-line.md`.\n\nChangelog: STEP import: a syntax error names the failing entity's #id and line instead of the DATA section (#912)\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #912\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
